28/03/2025
The deliverables for the ONERA ST7 are included in this folder, developed by group 2.
Analysis was performed on Boeing 767; an American wide-body airliner.

Contained within "3D_Models_Boeing_767" is:
    \--- the original model of the plane
    \--- the stl file of the skin of the model

Four meshes were developed, ranging from 1, the most coarse, to 4, the most fine.
Within each mesh_refinement_level_X, there is:
\--------- the stl file and the vtk file of the skin of the model
\--------------- Simulation results for each inclination around the plane 
                (-60,-40,-20,0,20,40,60)
\----------------------- the vtk file (in unstructured mesh and ASCII
format) of the volume of the model
\----------------------- a .bp folder of the results of the 3D simulation (pressure and velocity fields)
            The .bp file can be opened in paraview by opening the folder itself through paraview.

Within Scripts, there exists the python files used to obtain the results of
    the 3D simulations. In particular, the main.py script was used primarily to run the 
    stokes solver in parallel on the CentraleSupelec DCE clusters.

